# Speaker protection firmware verified on the reference phone
# (/usr/share/omamobile-audio/verified-firmware; device/cheetah/AOC-PLAN.md,
# "C9 for every phone with verified firmware").
#
# One line per verified firmware: the system (the DT's cirrus,subsystem-id),
# the digest omamobile-speaker-protection computes over Google's protection
# firmware and both speaker tunings (fw_digest: cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot-<system>
# .wmfw, -top.bin and -bottom.bin, as tools/extract-vendor-firmware installs
# them from the owner's factory image), then a note: where and when it was
# verified. Stage auto runs c9 (817, analog 14 bottom / 11 top) on a phone
# with aoc_alsa_dev speaker_protection=1 whose installed firmware has a digest
# listed here, or with its own C9a stamp; media otherwise. The digest is
# Google's files' and the same on every phone extracted from the same files;
# it identifies no phone, and no file is shipped.
#
# A digest goes here only after the attended C9a procedure passed with
# exactly those files on the reference phone (`omamobile-speaker-protection
# verify` wrote a stamp for it), and the c9 levels were heard and watched
# with music ("C9 with real music"). Read it on that phone with
#   omamobile-speaker-protection digest
# (or `sed -n 's/^firmware //p' /var/lib/omamobile/speaker-protection-verified`,
# which is the stamp's own copy). Never type one from memory or from another
# phone's files that weren't verified.
#
# Format: SYSTEM DIGEST NOTE   (64 lowercase hex digits; '#' starts a comment)
#
# TODO(maintainer): the reference 7 Pro's digest was not recorded in
# AOC-PLAN; add its line from `omamobile-speaker-protection digest` on that
# phone, e.g. "cheetah <64 hex digits> reference 7 Pro, C9a 2026-10-12,
# c9 levels 2026-10-31". Until then no phone gets c9 from this list.
